2,Levuka - Wikipedia,https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Levuka,"February 20, 2025 - At the census in 2007, the last to date, Levuka town had a population of 1,131 (plus 3,266 living in the peri-urban area as defined by the Bureau of Statistics), about half of Ovalau's 8,360 inhabitants. It is the economic hub and the largest of 24 settlements on the island.",Levuka,Austronesian
3,Ministry of Culture-Austronesian Music and Cultural Exchange,https://www.moc.gov.tw/en/cp.aspx?n=443,"It's a pity that Taiwanese aboriginal songs are rich and various yet there are only a few musical instruments. I found a few and compare them with the ones from Southeast Asia. We all know that twin-pipe nose flutes are only found in Taiwan, and they exist in Paiwan and are documented in Tsou's literature. The Austronesians in Southeast Asia have single-pipe nose flutes instead of twin-pipe nose flutes.",Levuka,Austronesian
